# What the ST prints reaches the RP intact: our ESC/P pages (TEXT.PRN and
# GRAPH.PRN, sent byte by byte through BIOS Bconout(0) by PRFILES from the
# floppy's AUTO folder) go through the hook, as 1 KB blocks and a last one
# sent when printing pauses, to the RP, which writes them as one job on its
# card, closed once its idle timeout has passed: equal to the two files byte
# for byte (the size and MD5 the RP logs as it closes the job, whose file is
# deleted once its PDF is written).
@disk-a tools/dev/builds/disks/escp.st
text "Machine +: (ST|STE|Mega STE), TOS" 1500
key e
wait 100
key 0x01
wait 900
key 0x39
jobbytes * 2938 3000
jobsame 1 tools/dev/builds/disks/escp-expected.prn
hookstate
